on.","citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c12"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c12"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c12","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.80 (An upper bound for the reset expression)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.80, p. 67, label record:257bm-c12","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Let $d\\ge5$ be an actual upper-reset row. Write $E_d$ for its reset charge, the sum of four times the adjacent upper overshoot and the corresponding nonnegative correction term. The upper-reset identity is\n$$\n\\mathrm{rem}(d+1)+E_d=2^{d+1}.\n$$\nThe nonnegativity of the successor remainder therefore gives $E_d\\le2^{d+1}$, the side condition needed for Theorem 6.79. This argument uses the upper-reset branch assumption. It does not require the separate, conditional two-sided bound of Theorem 6.9, and does not assert the charge bound at arbitrary rows.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c12","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c12","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c12%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfUpperResetCriticalBand.seamUpperResetCharge_le%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c12%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.HalfUpperResetCriticalBand.seamUpperResetCharge_le%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.HalfUpperResetCriticalBand.seamUpperResetCharge_le"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.record-257bm-c12","i